"""LLVM as one shared library.

The mojo binary links against this rather than absorbing ~100 MB of LLVM
archives, and it is the piece an out-of-tree tool -- an IDE, a language server --
can link against without rebuilding LLVM itself.

Two things had to be true for this to work, both easy to lose:

1. LLVM must be compiled with default symbol visibility. The toolchain applies
   -fvisibility=hidden to everything (bazel/internal/cc-toolchain/args/BUILD.bazel:124),
   which leaves a dylib with tens of thousands of defined symbols and a couple
   of hundred exported. --config=release overrides it for this external path;
   see the per_file_copt in .bazelrc.

2. Every LLVM cc_library in the binary's transitive closure must be listed
   here. Anything left out gets linked statically into the binary as well, and
   two copies of LLVM in one process means two ManagedStatic registries and two
   sets of cl::opt -- which fails at startup, not at link time.

The dep list is the answer to

    bazel query 'kind("cc_library rule",
                      filter("llvm-project//llvm", deps(//KGEN/tools/mojo:mojo)))'

Regenerate it with that query if the compiler starts using a new LLVM library;
bazel will tell you, loudly, if one is missing. (rules_cc calls this attribute
'deps' -- it was 'roots' until recently, and the error for the old name is
clear about it.)
"""

load("@rules_cc//cc:defs.bzl", "cc_shared_library")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

cc_shared_library(
    name = "LLVM",
    shared_lib_name = "libLLVM.dylib",
    # Export everything LLVM defines: consumers outside this build (the IDE)
    # need symbols that nothing inside it happens to call.
    exports_filter = [
        "@llvm-project//llvm:__subpackages__",
        # LLVM's Support links zlib-ng and zstd, so they end up inside this
        # dylib. Whatever else in the binary wants them has to get them from
        # here rather than linking a second copy; bazel refuses to guess and
        # asks to be told, which is what this is.
        # Canonical (@@...+) names: neither repo is a direct dependency of this
        # module, so the plain @zlib-ng form is not visible from here.
        "@@zlib-ng+//:__subpackages__",
        "@@zstd+//:__subpackages__",
    ],
    deps = [
        "@llvm-project//llvm:AArch64AsmParser",
        "@llvm-project//llvm:AArch64CodeGen",
        "@llvm-project//llvm:AArch64CommonTableGen",
